{"id": "sdqa0121", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 4.78, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.0891, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "n. When n is a positive integer, exponentiation corresponds to repeated multiplication of the base: that is, bn is the product of multiplying n bas", "query": "What is exponentiation?", "transcript": "What is exponentiation?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Exponentiation is a mathematical operation where a number, called the base, is multiplied by itself a certain number of times, which is called the exponent or power. For example, if you see 5 raised to the power of 3, written as 5³, that means 5 multiplied by itself three times, so 5 × 5 × 5 equals 125. The exponent tells you how many times the base is used as a factor in the multiplication.", "answer_ms": 2107}
{"id": "sdqa0124", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 3.37, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2482, "eot_read_ms": 17, "reference_answer": "is a Latin phrase that means \"of its (his, her, their) own kind; in a class by itself; unique", "query": "What does sui generis mean?", "transcript": "What does sui generis mean?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Sui Generis means unique or one-of-a-kind.", "answer_ms": 240}
